was the lizard a waste of cgi does  electro's makeover make the cut we put  spider-man's villains at a head-to-head  showdown to answer one question who's  the best at being bad  in spider-man no way home willem dafoe  alfred molina thomas hayden church reese  e fans and jamie foxx are all back in  their respective roles as the green  goblin doctor octopus the sandman the  lizard and electro it's time to line up  this quintet of antagonists and rank the  maddest baddest villains in spider-man  no way home  scale obsessed scientist dr kirk connors  was the first foe of andrew garfield  spider-man back in 2012's the amazing  spider-man the lizard returns in  spider-man no way home but has the least  screen time of all the villains not even  warranting a worthy entrance his arrival  happens off-screen after he's captured  by doctor strange while peter is dealing  with electro and sandman from there he's  left in the van for a lengthy portion of  the film before being a forgetful cgi  beastie chasing after the webslinger  even the method of putting him out of  action is identical to his demise in the  amazing spider-man sadly the lizard  feels like a plus one only there to  build out the numbers  the triple threat that rounds off the  original group of cinematic spider-man  villains comes in the form of flint  marco also known as the sandman last  seen making amends for pasdees and toby  maguire's spider-man 3 marco is still a  danger to this particular wall crawler  although not nearly as much as the rest  in the lineup while prominent for most  of the film his presence does raise a  few questions in the final act that sees  him fighting against our heroes for  reasons that aren't too clear instead  he's only put to the forefront when it's  time for him to burst into action while  still a feast for the eyes the sandman  makes for an ill-fitting piece to the  much grander puzzle of no way home  if all the foes are face off against  spider-man and no way home electro is  without a doubt the one that's had the  most drastic change since the last time  we saw him in the amazing spider-man 2.  jamie foxx's original iteration was a  bumbling scientist with a comb over but  the maxwell dylan we're reunited with  here is quite simply much more like the  actor that plays him somehow dylan's  time in the grid after his failed effort  to become pure energy has turned him  into one of the few criminals and this  group you might want to hang out with  that being said his obsession with a new  form of energy does make him a force to  be reckoned with making him an excellent  fit for third place  spider-man's enigmatic enemy and  director sam raimi's original trilogy dr  otto octavius is just as charming and  equally chilling upon his return in  spider-man no way home wait no seriously  what's your actual name  and unsurprisingly alfred molina's  portrayal of the scientists we've not  seen him play for 17 years is seamless  from his scattered memories of a  fistfight with spider-man to battling  with the voices in his head molina makes  it crystal clear why his performance in  spider-man 2 made him one of the best  comic book movie villains in history we  know that octavius resorted to violence  and criminal means to achieve his goal  but we still manage to see the flicker  of a good man in his final moments in no  way home more time is spent ensuring  that the seemingly lost cause is found  and sticks around a little longer  darkhog feels almost scrooge-like here  before learning the error of his ways  making his turn back to the light a joy  to see  no one gives their character more  attention or advancement than willem  dafoe as norman osborne also known as  the green goblin the first foe of toby  maguire's spider-man could have easily  phoned in his performance instead he  gets back into both mindsets as a man  and the monster controlling him making  him one of the most formidable enemies  holland spidey has faced in spider-man  no way home taking the iconic but  performance limiting mask out of the  equation makes a split between osborne  and green goblin so much more potent and  petrifying holland's hero is pushed to  his limits by a monster on a glider that  effortlessly gets inside his head  there's no denying that the mcu has  hosted many great villains over the  years but green goblin reminds us that  he helped set the bar long before the  universe even existed  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  spider-man no way home are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and to  the bell so you don't miss a single one  [Music]
 

